<title>USA: Unidigital Inc Q1 EPS falls on more shrs.</title>
<headline>Unidigital Inc Q1 EPS falls on more shrs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>UNIDIGITAL INC.</p>
<p>			CONSOLIDATED INCOME STATEMENT</p>
<p>		 FOR THE THREE MONTHS ENDED NOVEMBER 30</p>
<p>			     1996		   1995(a)</p>
<p>Net sales	   $  5,227,719	  $ 2,717,822</p>
<p>Net income	     $ 461,820	    $ 435,759</p>
<p>Net income per</p>
<p>  share		  $     .14	    $     .22</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding	  3,189,216	    2,000,000</p>
<p>			 See notes to financial statements</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) 1995 period reflects operations of combined predecessors.</p>
<p>Company previously operated as a subchapter S corporation, prior to its initial public offering February 1, 1996. In 1995, the company did not make a provision for federal corporate income taxes, since it was a subchapter S corporation.</p>
</text>
